/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  trayEfficiency05_chanFair_yanagi14  --  the EFFICIENCY OF A SIEVE TRAY COMPUTED FROM ITS
  GEOMETRY, compared with a commercial-scale measurement that is IN-SAMPLE for this
  correlation (Chan & Fair's data bank lists these FRI trays; nothing was fitted HERE)
  (DEV.md 4c C329).  Cyclohexane / n-heptane at 34 kPa, total reflux.

  THE TRAY: FRI's 14 % hole-area sieve tray (Table I): 1.2 m column, 610 mm spacing,
  12.7 mm holes on 30.2 mm triangular pitch, 1.5 mm plate, outlet weir 50.8 mm
  x 940 mm, downcomer 0.14 m2, hole area 0.118 m2.
  Source: Yanagi & Sakata, Ind. Eng. Chem. Process Des. Dev. 21 (1982) 712.
  The pair of this case is trayEfficiency02_yanagi08 (8 %): the two differ in the open area
  and in nothing else.

  THE MODEL.  The stages stay equilibrium stages; each tray's Murphree
  efficiency is computed by Chan & Fair, Ind. Eng. Chem. Process Des. Dev. 23
  (1984) 814, Eqs 9-26 (pp. 816-817): Bennett's clear liquid, the vapour-side
  volumetric coefficient k_V a_i = D_V^0.5 (1030 f - 867 f^2)/h_L^0.5 at the
  tray's approach to flood f, Foss-Gerster's liquid side, Barker & Self's eddy
  diffusion; then the entrainment loss (Colburn with Fair's median psi, Perry
  9ed 14-98/14-99), with the dry curve held flat above f = 0.6 as the paper
  prescribes.  The tray pressure drop is Bolles & Fair's (Perry 9ed
  14-100..14-109).

  MEASURED INPUTS (the paper): the tray geometry (Table I); the liquid
    viscosity 0.37 mPa s (Table II, 34 kPa -- the package carries no
    liquid viscosity for these components, so the paper's own average enters
    Wilke-Chang); the column pressure.
  ASSUMED: the reboiler liquid, 0.29 mol fraction cyclohexane (Table III gives
    0.284 and 0.294 for the two runs it lists; the other points' compositions
    are not published); every point of the sweep uses it.
  ESTIMATED PROPERTIES: vapour pressure (Antoine fits to CoolProp), ideal
    liquid, vapour viscosity (Chung, Vc from Zc(omega)), vapour diffusivity
    (Fuller; the diffusion volumes, Poling 5ed Table 11-1, are added to the
    case's own component records), liquid diffusivity (Wilke-Chang at
    infinite dilution, combined linearly, Poling 5ed Eq 11-10.2), liquid
    density (Rackett on the record's Vliq), surface tension (Brock-Bird).
  FITTED PARAMETERS: NONE.
  HELD-OUT POINTS: all -- Table III runs 628 (F 1.47, E_o 70.8 %, dP 0.393 kPa) and 625 (F 2.36,
    41.1 %, 0.858 kPa) -- TABULATED -- and the five 14 % points at ~30 kPa of
    Figure 12 and of Figure 13 (DIGITISED).
    The comparison table is in docs/design/c329-ratebased-first-delivery.md.
  WHAT WAS CHOSEN AFTER SEEING DATA, said so: the pressure-drop route.  The
    default (Sinnott) gave 0.79 kPa per tray on run 628 against the measured
    0.393; Bolles & Fair was then implemented from Perry and gives 0.41.  No
    number inside either correlation was touched.
  IN-SAMPLE: YES.  Chan & Fair's data bank (Table I, p. 816) lists the FRI
    trays of Yanagi & Sakata 1982 (14 %) and Sakata & Yanagi 1979 (8 %); the
    14 % runs at 165 and 1138 kPa are shown apart as not fitting (p. 818,
    Fig. 3).  Nothing in this case was fitted HERE, but the correlation saw
    these trays.

  WHAT THE MODEL SEES OF THE OPEN AREA: only the approach to flood f
  (Perry's open-area capacity correction makes the 8 % tray's f larger).
  Weeping is not modelled.  The sweep stops below the model's own
  entrainment flood (Fair's psi = 1).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        column;
        type        distillationColumn;
        model       totalReflux;

        operation
        {
            nStages        11;          // 10 trays + the reboiler
            P              34 kPa;
            condenser      { type total; }

            totalReflux
            {
                fFactor        1.47;    // swept; (m/s)(kg/m3)^0.5, reboiler vapour on the tower area
                specifiedAt    reboiler;
                composition
                {
                    cyclohexane    0.29;
                    nHeptane       0.71;
                }
            }

            efficiency
            {
                model            ChanFair;
                lightKey         cyclohexane;
                liquidViscosity  3.7e-4;   // Pa s, Yanagi & Sakata Table II, 34 kPa
                entrainment      FairMedian;
            }

            hydraulics
            {
                trayType               sieve;
                pressureDropModel      BollesFair;   // Perry 9ed 14-100..14-109
                diameter               1.2;      // m  (Table I)
                traySpacing            0.610;    // m  (Table I)
                weirHeight             0.0508;   // m  (Table I, efficiency runs)
                holeDiameter           0.0127;   // m  (Table I)
                holeAreaFraction       0.1387;   // 0.118 m2 holes / 0.851 m2 active (Table I)
                downcomerAreaFraction  0.1238;   // 0.14 m2 / 1.131 m2 (Table I)
                weirLengthFraction     0.7833;   // 0.940 m / 1.2 m (Table I)
                orificeCoefficient     0.693;    // Perry 9ed Eq 14-102a: 0.74 A_h/A_a + exp(0.29 (1.5/12.7) - 0.56)
            }
        }
    }
);
